# Line endings, pinned so a Windows checkout does not change the bytes.
#
# The repository builds for windows/amd64, so contributors on Windows are expected. Git's own
# default there (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites text to CRLF on checkout, which is wrong for two
# kinds of file here:
#
#   - Go sources: gofmt accepts CRLF, but every diff then shows whole-file changes when a
#     Windows contributor touches a line, and `gofmt -l` reports clean while the file differs.
#   - Shell snippets inside the justfile and the Python scripts: a trailing \r is part of the
#     last argument, so a path becomes "out.gguf\r" and the tool cannot find it.
#
# `text=auto` asks Git to detect text and store it with LF; the explicit entries below name the
# types where that detection is worth being certain about.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.go   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
justfile    text eol=lf
.gitignore  text eol=lf
.editorconfig text eol=lf

# Model files are large binaries a contributor may keep beside the tree; nothing here should
# ever try to diff or merge them.
*.gguf binary

# Test executables and archives are binary by nature.
*.test   binary
*.out    binary
*.prof   binary
